stify-content:flex-end;text-align:right}@media(max-width:768px){.mw-parser-output .wst-header-mainblock{flex-wrap:wrap}.mw-parser-output .wst-header-central-cell{flex:0 0 100%;order:-2;width:auto}.mw-parser-output .wst-header-back,.mw-parser-output .wst-header-forward{width:auto}}.mw-parser-output .wst-header-notes{display:inline-block;border-collapse:collapse;border-spacing:0;empty-cells:hide;font-size:.9em;line-height:1.4;margin:0 auto 4px auto;width:100%}.mw-parser-output .wst-header-left{float:left}</style><div class=\"ws-header wst-header-structure wst-unknown wst-header ws-header ws-noexport noprint dynlayout-exempt\"><div class=\"wst-header-mainblock wst-unknown-mainblock headertemplate\"><div class=\"wst-header-back searchaux wst-unknown-back\"><div class=\"wst-header-back-arrow\">\u2190</div><div class=\"wst-header-back-link\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Ch%27%C3%AAn_Ming-hsia\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Ch&#39;\u00ean Ming-hsia\">Ch'\u00ean Ming-hsia</a></div></div><div class=\"wst-header-central-cell wst-unknown-central-cell\"><span class=\"wst-header-title wst-unknown-title\"><span class=\"wst-header-title-text\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period\">Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period</a>, Volume 1</span><br class=\"wst-header-title-break\" /><span class=\"contributor-text\">edited by&#160;<span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"/wiki/Author:Arthur_W._Hummel\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Author:Arthur W. Hummel\">Arthur W. Hummel</a></span></span><div class=\"header-section-text\">Ch&#39;\u00ean P&#39;\u00eang-nien <span class=\"contributor-text\">by&#160;<span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"/wiki/Author:C._P._Wong\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Author:C. P. Wong\">C. P. Wong</a></span></span></div></span></div><div class=\"wst-header-forward searchaux wst-unknown-forward\"><div class=\"wst-header-forward-link\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Ch%27%C3%AAn_Shih-kuan\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Ch&#39;\u00ean Shih-kuan\">Ch'\u00ean Shih-kuan</a></div><div class=\"wst-header-forward-arrow\">\u2192</div></div></div><div class=\"wst-header-notes header&#95;notes searchaux wst-unknown-notes\"><style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r14791120\">.mw-parser-output .plainSister{display:block;font-size:93%;line-height:normal;list-style-type:none;list-style-image:none;list-style-position:outside;border:1px solid var(--border-color-interactive--hover,#AAA);float:right;clear:right;margin:0.5ex 0 0.5ex 0.5ex;padding:0;background:var(--background-color-base,#FFFFFF);color:var(--color-base,#202122)}.mw-parser-output .sisicon,.mw-parser-output .dabicon{padding-right:1ex}</style><ul class=\"plainSister\"><li class=\"sisitem\"><span class=\"sisicon\"><span typeof=\"mw:File/Frameless\"><a href=\"/wiki/Special:SiteMatrix\" title=\"Special:SiteMatrix\"><img alt=\"Sister Projects\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Wikimedia-logo.svg/20px-Wikimedia-logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikisource.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Wikimedia-logo.svg/40px-Wikimedia-logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikisource.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"1024\" data-file-height=\"1024\" /></a></span></span><a href=\"/wiki/Special:SiteMatrix\" title=\"Special:SiteMatrix\">sister projects</a>: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chen_Pengnian\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Chen Pengnian\">Wikipedia article</a>, <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q107367046\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"d:Q107367046\">Wikidata item</a></li></ul></div><div class=\"ws-noexport\" id=\"ws-data\" style=\"speak:none\"><span id=\"ws-article-id\">3634069</span><span id=\"ws-title\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period\">Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period</a>, Volume 1 \u2014 Ch&#39;\u00ean P&#39;\u00eang-nien</span><span id=\"ws-editor\">Arthur W. Hummel</span><span id=\"ws-author\">C. P. Wong</span></div></div>\n<p><span style=\"display:none\" id=\"dynamic&#95;layout&#95;overrider\">Layout 2</span>\n</p>\n<div class=\"prp-pages-output\" lang=\"en\">\n<p><span><span class=\"pagenum ws-pagenum\" id=\"95\" data-page-number=\"95\" data-page-name=\"Page:Eminent Chinese Of The Ch\u2019ing Period - Hummel - 1943 - Vol. 1.pdf/107\" data-page-index=\"107\" data-page-quality=\"4\" title=\"Page:Eminent&#95;Chinese&#95;Of&#95;The&#95;Ch%E2%80%99ing&#95;Period&#95;-&#95;Hummel&#95;-&#95;1943&#95;-&#95;Vol.&#95;1.pdf/107\"><span id=\"pageindex&#95;107\" class=\"pagenum-inner ws-noexport\">&#8203;</span></span></span><b>CH'\u00caN</b> P'\u00eang-nien \u9673\u9d6c\u5e74 (<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r14767791\">.mw-parser-output .wst-tooltip{cursor:help;border-bottom:thin dotted cornflowerblue}.mw-parser-output .wst-tooltip-nodash{border-bottom:none}</style><span class=\"wst-tooltip wst-tooltip-dash\" title=\"Courtesy name (Tz\u00fb/Zi, \u5b57)\">T.</span>&#160;\u5317\u6e9f and \u6ec4\u6d32) Jan. 10, 1664\u20131723, Feb. 9, official, was a native of Hsiang-t'an, Hunan. In his youth his family retired to the mountains to avoid disturbances following the revolt of <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Wu_San-kuei\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Wu San-kuei\">Wu San-kuei</a></span>&#32;[<i>q.&#8239;v.</i>]. There he engaged in the study of the classics. When the family returned to Hsiang-t'an he took the examinations, finally receiving his <i>chin-shih</i> degree in Peking in 1691. Five years later he was appointed magistrate of Hsi-an, Chekiang, and then of Shan-yang, Kiangsu. He achieved a reputation as a model official with the appellation \"Ch'\u00ean Ch'ing-t'ien\" \u9673\u9752\u5929 (Ch'\u00ean of the Clear Sky) because of his&#32;<span><span class=\"pagenum ws-pagenum\" id=\"96\" data-page-number=\"96\" data-page-name=\"Page:Eminent Chinese Of The Ch\u2019ing Period - Hummel - 1943 - Vol. 1.pdf/108\" data-page-index=\"108\" data-page-quality=\"4\" title=\"Page:Eminent&#95;Chinese&#95;Of&#95;The&#95;Ch%E2%80%99ing&#95;Period&#95;-&#95;Hummel&#95;-&#95;1943&#95;-&#95;Vol.&#95;1.pdf/108\"><span id=\"pageindex&#95;108\" class=\"pagenum-inner ws-noexport\">&#8203;</span></span></span>honesty, frugality, and good sense. When he was prefect of Nanking (1703\u201305) his superior, A\u0161an (\u963f\u5c71, d. 1714), governor-general of Kiangsu, motivated by jealousy, falsely accused him of bribery in connection with revenue and taxation, and of impropriety in establishing lecture-halls on sites that had previously been utilized for houses of prostitution. Although sentenced to die, he was granted imperial pardon. Convinced of his innocence, the emperor summoned him to Peking where he was placed on the commission to edit the anthology of Sung, Chin, Y\u00fcan, and Ming poetry, \u56db\u671d\u8a69 <i>Ss\u016d-ch'ao shih</i>, which was printed in 1709 in 312 <i>ch\u00fcan</i>.\n</p><p>In 1708 he was appointed prefect of Soochow and in the following year, acting-financial commissioner of Kiangsu. <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Gali\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Gali\">Gali</a></span>&#32;[<i>q.&#8239;v.</i>], governor-general of Kiangsu, accused him in 1711 of treason for a poem, entitled \u864e\u90b1 <i>Hu-ch'iu</i>, which he had written concerning a hillock of that name located seven <i>li</i> northwest of Soochow. This accusation was likewise disallowed by the emperor who again summoned him to Peking. This time (1719\u20131722) he served on the editorial board that compiled the phrase dictionary, <i>F\u00ean-lei tz\u016d chin</i> (see under <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Ho_Ch%27o\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Ho Ch&#39;o\">Ho Ch'o</a></span>). Later he was ordered to assist <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Chang_P%27%C3%AAng-ko\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Chang P&#39;\u00eang-ko\">Chang P'\u00eang-ko</a></span>&#32;[<i>q.&#8239;v.</i>] in a survey of the Grand Canal, and in 1721 was made director-general of Yellow River Conservancy in Honan, which post he held until his death in 1723. He was canonized as K'o-ch'in \u606a\u52e4. His collected prose works, \u9053\u69ae\u5802\u6587\u96c6 <i>Tao-Jung-t'ang w\u00ean-chi</i>, in 6 <i>ch\u00fcan</i>, and his verse, <i>Tao jung-t'ang</i> (\u8a69)-<i>chi</i> in 10 <i>ch\u00fcan</i>, were printed, together with his <i>nien-p'u</i>, in 1762. An edition of his collected works, entitled <i>Ch'\u00ean K'o-ch'in chi</i>, in 39 <i>ch\u00fcan</i>, is listed in the <i>Imperial Catalogue</i> (see under <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Chi_Y%C3%BCn\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Chi Y\u00fcn\">Chi Y\u00fcn</a></span>). A treatise on public administration, \u6b77\u4ed5\u653f\u7565 <i>Li shih ch\u00eang l\u00fceh</i>, in 1 <i>ch\u00fcan</i>, and rules and regulations for river conservancy, \u6cb3\u5de5\u689d\u7d04 <i>Ho-kung t'iao-y\u00fceh</i>, also in 1 <i>ch\u00fcan</i>, were both written shortly before his death.\n</p>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r15431518\">.mw-parser-output .wst-rule{background-color:currentcolor;color:inherit;width:auto;margin:2px auto 2px auto;height:1px;overflow:hidden}.mw-parser-output .wst-rule.wst-rule-left{margin-left:0}.mw-parser-output .wst-rule.wst-rule-right{margin-right:0}.mw-parser-output .wst-rule.__uirule{background-color:#a2a9b1;color:inherit;border:0;margin-top:0.2em;margin-bottom:0.2em}</style><hr class=\"wst-rule wst-rule-left\" style=\"color:inherit;width:40%;\" />\n<p>[1/283/6b; 3/164/1a; 23/16/1a; \u6e56\u5357\u6587\u5fb5 <i>Hunan w\u00ean-ch\u00eang</i> 32/1, 61/59; <i>Ss\u016d-k'u</i> (see under <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Chi_Y%C3%BCn\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Chi Y\u00fcn\">Chi Y\u00fcn</a></span>) 184/2b; <i>Hsiang-t'an-hsien chih</i> (1889) <i>ch\u00fcan</i> 8, sec. 4/81a.]\n</p>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r15431519\">.mw-parser-output .wst-right{text-align:right}</style><div class=\"wst-right\" style=\"margin-right:2em;\">\n<p><span class=\"smallcaps\" style=\"font-variant:small-caps;\">C. P. Wong</span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<p><br />\n&#32;\n</p>\n</div>\n</div>"},"links":[{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Ch'\u00ean Ming-hsia"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Ch'\u00ean Shih-kuan"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Chang P'\u00eang-ko"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Chi Y\u00fcn"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Gali"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Ho Ch'o"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Wu San-kuei"},{"ns":102,"exists":"","*":"Author:Arthur W. Hummel"},{"ns":102,"exists":"","*":"Author:C. P. Wong"}],"sections":[],"wikitext":{"*":"{{Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period\n | volume   = 1\n | onlysection = ch'en p'eng-nien\n | previous = Ch'\u00ean Ming-hsia\n | next     = Ch'\u00ean Shih-kuan\n | from     = 107\n | to       = 108\n | notes    = \n | section_author = C. P. Wong\n}}{{DEFAULTSORT:Ch'\u00ean P'\u00eang-nien}}"}}}